{"kind":"artifact","text":".github/workflows at exact clean pushed head 38af668ff465dbd05ab1fdf3d3d2cd3290a2a8f1 (branch request/repo-security-gates).\n\nCI runs make ui-check rather than make ui: the existing reproducibility gate cannot cover a stale embed, because Vite emits content-hashed filenames so a rebuilt bundle lands as a new untracked file and git diff --exit-code ignores untracked files. security.yml adds govulncheck pinned by module version and the secret scanner, on a weekly schedule as well as per-push, and no longer fetches full history.\n\nAnswering child request be158c2e under promise 15999b98, after codex's ratified changes-requested 5c7167fe. Replaces the four artifacts at head 01d602d5, all retired.\n\nEvery finding was correct and each is fixed.\n\nThe blocking one cost a round rather than a defect: verify-preview-clone.sh still contained a recursive force delete, so codex declined to execute the scripts or the full gate set. I had flagged it and asked rather than acting, and a known blocker left in place blocks the reviewer as surely as the code. It now clears its fixture with bounded find, and the explanatory comment was reworded after I noticed it still contained the forbidden string - which the condition also prohibits.\n\nI was wrong about YAML and conceded on evidence. I had argued a real parser was not worth the supply-chain cost and measured nine new go.sum lines. The measurement was right and the inference was wrong: those lines name four modules that are yaml.v3's own test dependencies, and go list -deps shows none of them enter the build graph. Nothing new is compiled or shipped. internal/ciguard now decodes YAML, and the rewrite is not cosmetic - two mutations that the previous text matching passed are now refused: a commit pin sitting in a comment above a tag-referenced action, and make ui-check commented out above a live make ui. It also catches a duplicate Dependabot ecosystem where the later entry silently wins.\n\nScanner repairs, all as directed. No exclusions at all, since the fixtures are assembled at runtime and an exclusion is a hole somebody can hide a secret in. The duplicated OpenSSH rule is gone. Fixtures for github_pat_ and sk- exercise two patterns that previously had none. And the test asserts the scanner's diagnostic rather than a nonzero exit: a scanner that crashed also exits nonzero, and reading that as a detection would let a broken gate report that it catches things. Injecting an early exit now makes twelve cases fail where they previously read as successful detections.\n\nsecurity.yml no longer fetches full history, so the workflow and the scanner make one scope claim rather than two.\n\nGates at this exact clean pushed head: go test ./... ok, go vet clean, make docs clean, make ui-check clean, verify-preview-clone.sh runs clean, git diff --check clean, worktree clean, branch on origin.\n\nSECURITY.md remains untouched and its public_surface_test gate stands.","body":{"commit":"38af668ff465dbd05ab1fdf3d3d2cd3290a2a8f1","path":".github/workflows"}}